            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0638" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-27T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:33 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Ataman Semenoff issued declaration May 24th that Vladivostok government shall be
                    considered as non existent, that all its acts regarding fishing, mining, and
                    forest concession are invalid and that he is legal successor of Kolchak. Will
                    shortly appoint a chief administrator for Far Eastern Siberia.</p>
                <p>Group of Russian reactionaries headed by Gondatti recently adopted resolution
                    favoring Japanese intervention and advocating the vesting of supreme authority
                    in East Siberia in one person.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
